With thousands of people driven from their homes by a massive flash flood that swept entire villages away, FRANCE 24 visits a school in Nepal's remote Rasuwa district that has been converted to a temporary shelter for the dispossessed. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d75e6228-a907-11f1-b550-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260905-100138-100414-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d75e6228-a907-11f1-b550-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260905-100138-100414-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">61d66626-a90d-11f1-9655-456b2dea8570</guid><pubDate>Sat, 05 Sep 2026 10:16:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d75e6228-a907-11f1-b550-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260905-100138-100414-CS.jpg">© FRANCE 24 screen capture</source><dc:creator>Shahzaib WAHLAH</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Germany: AfD eyes historic state election win</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260905-germany-afd-eyes-historic-state-election-win</link><description>
In Saxony-Anhalt, AfD – Germany's far-right party – is polling at 40% or more of voting intentions, just days ahead of the regional election on 6 September 2026. If the AfD wins an absolute majority of seats, it could soon be in charge here. It would be the first time since 1945 that a far-right party has led a German region.
 
To get there, the party is banking on the promise of a return to "the Germany of old", leaning on East German symbols such as Simson mopeds and retro aesthetics. It is a well-established strategy that draws on a gnawing sense of decline for decades and increasing distrust of traditional parties.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fe6073c4-a90d-11f1-9ce3-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260905-090812-091057-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fe6073c4-a90d-11f1-9ce3-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260905-090812-091057-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0415816a-a90e-11f1-9afb-456b2dea8570</guid><pubDate>Sat, 05 Sep 2026 09:58:46 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nepal: Temporary education centres help flood-displaced children</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260905-nepal-temporary-education-centres-help-flood-displaced-children</link><description>
Children displaced by flash floods in Nepal are attending a temporary education centre in Nuwakot, while aid organisations work to support devastated communities.
 
The UN estimates that $158 million worth of buildings have been damaged, with Nepal warning that reconstruction could cost billions.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d239c638-a908-11f1-9639-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260905-100437-100626-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d239c638-a908-11f1-9639-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260905-100437-100626-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d6c106a8-a908-11f1-90d1-79a19839b1c1</guid><pubDate>Sat, 05 Sep 2026 09:20:03 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Monaco rally to edge winless PSG and reclaim top spot</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20260905-monaco-rally-to-edge-winless-psg-and-reclaim-top-spot</link><description>
Monaco made it three wins on the trot and reclaimed the top spot by beating Paris Saint-Germain, who were playing their first home match of the season. Luis Enrique's men have now gone four matches without a win.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a7415736-a8ca-11f1-bd2d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/J24-Monaco-21.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a7415736-a8ca-11f1-bd2d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/J24-Monaco-21.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bdb8db94-a8cd-11f1-bcbc-d9c8cc477580</guid><pubDate>Sat, 05 Sep 2026 09:16:50 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>L'Equipe TV</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Trump sends envoys to Moscow, Kyiv with new plan to 'end war'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260905-trump-sends-envoys-to-moscow-kyiv-with-new-plan-to-end-war</link><description>
US President Donald Trump said Friday he is sending envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner to Moscow and Kyiv with a plan to end more than four years of war in Ukraine.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/240326ee-a909-11f1-9cb9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260905-100700-100838-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/240326ee-a909-11f1-9cb9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260905-100700-100838-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">29272b52-a909-11f1-95fb-79a19839b1c1</guid><pubDate>Sat, 05 Sep 2026 09:15:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Two senior Reform UK officials resign as Farage faces fresh foreign donations scandal</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260905-two-senior-reform-uk-officials-resign-as-farage-faces-fresh-foreign-donations-scandal</link><description>
Two senior officials from the hard-right Reform UK party stepped down Friday following a hidden-camera investigation that appeared to show them soliciting substantial foreign funding for party-commissioned opinion polls and a potential £500,000 donation from a US donor – banned under UK law. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/87346bd8-a8f0-11f1-953e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-04T171750Z-776567773-RC2GCNAQ5SJA-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-POLITICS-REFORM-CONFERENCE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/87346bd8-a8f0-11f1-953e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-04T171750Z-776567773-RC2GCNAQ5SJA-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-POLITICS-REFORM-CONFERENCE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">09d12000-a8f0-11f1-909d-05b1b8237714</guid><pubDate>Sat, 05 Sep 2026 06:30:29 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/87346bd8-a8f0-11f1-953e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-04T171750Z-776567773-RC2GCNAQ5SJA-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-POLITICS-REFORM-CONFERENCE.jpg">© Temilade Adelaja, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Middle East live: Explosions of unknown origin heard near Iran's Kharg Island</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260905-middle-east-live-israeli-strikes-on-south-and-east-lebanon-kill-three-people</link><description>
A correspondent for the semi-official Fars news agency on Saturday reported hearing explosions of unknown origin near Iran's Kharg Island in ‌the Gulf, ⁠a key oil terminal. The state-affiliated Nournews said there were unconfirmed reports ‌from local sources that an Iranian tanker ‌had been targeted by a missile fired by US forces. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/42236796-a8fb-11f1-8f34-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A3MJ99E-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/42236796-a8fb-11f1-8f34-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A3MJ99E-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9e9b199a-a8e4-11f1-9cc9-ed32b8bec523</guid><pubDate>Sat, 05 Sep 2026 05:01:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/42236796-a8fb-11f1-8f34-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A3MJ99E-1.jpg">© European Space Agency via AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Trump sends envoys to Moscow and Kyiv with new plan to 'end the war'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260905-trump-sends-envoys-to-moscow-and-kyiv-with-new-plan-to-end-the-war</link><description>
US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner are travelling to Moscow and Kyiv this weekend with what US President Donald Trump says is a new proposal to end the war in Ukraine. Despite Trump's promises to resolve the conflict, Washington's efforts to broker a peace have so far come to nothing.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b490ef0c-a8d2-11f1-8453-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/48f6682df0de12a6db7d992902ed511594a054fb.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b490ef0c-a8d2-11f1-8453-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/48f6682df0de12a6db7d992902ed511594a054fb.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b61cf636-a8d2-11f1-a249-151e03936e21</guid><pubDate>Sat, 05 Sep 2026 02:37:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b490ef0c-a8d2-11f1-8453-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/48f6682df0de12a6db7d992902ed511594a054fb.jpg">© Urs Flueeler, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>Uber withdraws from Nigeria</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/uber-withdraws-from-nigeria</link><description>
In tonight's programme, a UN report says foreign fighters and support networks are fuelling Sudan’s war and worsening violence against civilians. Also, Uber is pulling out of Nigeria and Uganda, leaving thousands of drivers scrambling for new sources of income. And finally, we discuss the festival with co-director Diarah N’Daw-Spech and Laurence Cole, co-producer of the Nigerian film "Shadow of Greed".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/65d6d146-a8a1-11f1-9963-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-13640605226a9b2da1479d08-40791610.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/65d6d146-a8a1-11f1-9963-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-13640605226a9b2da1479d08-40791610.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5786c5e8-a8a0-11f1-8f6e-c70340fa1871</guid><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 20:39:08 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Hélène Daouphars</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>‘Major potential breaches of British election law’: Inside Channel 4’s investigation into Reform UK</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260904-major-potential-breaches-of-british-election-law-understanding-channel-4-s-investigation</link><description>
