German Interior Minister Alexander Dobrindt on Friday said the evidence in a recent spate of sabotage attacks on power grids across the country points to a militant climate activist. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4e429a5c-a87d-11f1-9a14-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7473G4.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4e429a5c-a87d-11f1-9a14-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7473G4.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ce3da0ba-a88e-11f1-9b83-4b7169375ee5</guid><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 18:40:07 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4e429a5c-a87d-11f1-9a14-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7473G4.jpg">© Ina Fassbender, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Earth</category><title>UN ditches Mercator map to adopt more accurate one reflecting Africa's true size</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/earth/20260904-un-ditches-mercator-map-to-adopt-more-accurate-one-reflecting-africa-s-true-size</link><description>
The UN General Assembly on Friday voted to shift away from the 16th-century Mercator map, designed by Flemish cartographer Gerardus Mercator, for a more accurate one reflecting the true size of continents. The resolution, spearheaded by several African countries and co-sponsored by France, was backed by 164 countries. The US voted against and six other states abstained.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b8def100-a88a-11f1-98da-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/equal-earth.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b8def100-a88a-11f1-98da-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/equal-earth.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6703af86-a88c-11f1-a27b-0f01ce9047e8</guid><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 18:31:21 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b8def100-a88a-11f1-98da-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/equal-earth.jpg">© Screengrab equal-earth.com</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The World This Week</category><title>Germany’s ‘Most Dangerous Man’: PR gift for the AfD?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20260904-germany-s-most-dangerous-man-pr-gift-for-the-afd</link><description>
The Ukrainian capital was hit by Russia’s most intense wave of air attacks on Kyiv, reportedly in four years, with Reuters describing air raid sirens, drones, cruise and ballistic missiles exhausting Ukraine’s defence system, with 12 people killed and the Ukrainian foreign minister making a direct appeal to Western allies for more Patriot interceptor missiles.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/33774712-a7c0-11f1-929c-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T230341Z-762856586-RC2V9NAQ6F54-RTRMADP-3-GERMANY-ELECTION-SAXONY-ANHALT-AFD-CANDIDATE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/33774712-a7c0-11f1-929c-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T230341Z-762856586-RC2V9NAQ6F54-RTRMADP-3-GERMANY-ELECTION-SAXONY-ANHALT-AFD-CANDIDATE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ade4f552-a88e-11f1-b5b6-0f01ce9047e8</guid><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 18:31:15 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Gavin LEE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israel's West Bank camp displacements could be crime against humanity, UN says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260904-israel-s-west-bank-camp-displacements-could-be-crime-against-humanity-un-says</link><description>
The Israeli government's forced displacement of the entire populations of three West Bank refugee camps in January 2025 could amount to crimes against humanity, a UN report warned Friday. More than 33,000 Palestinians forced out of the Jenin, Nur Shams and Tulkarm camps have not been permitted to return home. Israel slammed the report for "spreading misinformation".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7cd77414-a878-11f1-bbf1-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25050234334915.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7cd77414-a878-11f1-bbf1-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25050234334915.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9d75c9d6-a879-11f1-9f3f-9d5ffd1b430b</guid><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 16:26:55 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7cd77414-a878-11f1-bbf1-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25050234334915.jpg">© Majdi Mohammed, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>US midterms start with North Carolina distributing mail-voting ballots</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260904-us-midterms-begin-with-chaos-over-mail-voting-crackdown</link><description>
North Carolina on Friday became the first state authorised to begin sending out ballots, formally launching the 2026 US midterms as President Donald Trump’s administration fights to impose sweeping restrictions on the practice.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d11236ee-a662-11f1-9ae7-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/bb30b5bf37e781f443665b25112221e81b7c2d36.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d11236ee-a662-11f1-9ae7-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/bb30b5bf37e781f443665b25112221e81b7c2d36.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bd7ebe96-a878-11f1-ad8a-9d5ffd1b430b</guid><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 15:53:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d11236ee-a662-11f1-9ae7-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/bb30b5bf37e781f443665b25112221e81b7c2d36.jpg">© Saul Loeb, AFP (File)</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Italian opposition fragmented: No alternative leader, no other possible leader than Giorgia Meloni'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-italian-opposition-fragmented-no-alternative-leader-no-other-possible-leader-than-giorgia-meloni-1</link><description>
Alison Sargent is pleased to welcome Political analyst Lorenzo Pregliasco, co-founder of polling agency YouTrend and adjunct professor at the University of Bologna. He argues that Giorgia Meloni’s unusual longevity in office is best understood not simply as a record of political strength, but as the product of a carefully calibrated governing strategy. Meloni has maintained stability partly by avoiding structural reforms disruptive enough to mobilize multiple constituencies against her at once. Her dominance within Fratelli d’Italia, the absence of a credible alternative leader, and a fragmented opposition have reinforced that advantage.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/853e8964-a871-11f1-a821-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260904-080636-081309-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/853e8964-a871-11f1-a821-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260904-080636-081309-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8a679b7e-a871-11f1-98cc-8948df265a00</guid><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 15:35:05 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Germany: Hans-Thomas Tillschneider, the ideologist behind the AFD’s plans in Saxony-Anhalt</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260904-germany-hans-thomas-tillschneider-the-ideologist-behind-the-afd-s-plans-in-saxony-anhalt</link><description>
The far-right German political party Alternative for Germany could win a historical victory in the eastern state of Saxony-Anhalt in key elections this Sunday. The party’s agenda is more radical than ever and inspired by the proposals of an influential ideologist in the region: Hans-Thomas Tillschneider.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d6490a76-a6e3-11f1-a0d9-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Tillschneider.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d6490a76-a6e3-11f1-a0d9-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Tillschneider.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b9f29088-a86c-11f1-a0db-fb41f6dfc750</guid><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 15:34:36 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d6490a76-a6e3-11f1-a0d9-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Tillschneider.jpg">© Jens Schluter, AFP</source><dc:creator>Sébastian SEIBT</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Trump envoys Witkoff, Kushner to visit Russia and Ukraine in coming days</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-trump-envoys-witkoff-kushner-to-visit-russia-and-ukraine-in-coming-days</link><description>
US President Donald Trump's envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner are expected to arrive in Kyiv for a first-time visit on Sunday, several sources reported. Witkoff and Kushner – Trump's son-in-law – have been involved in shuttle diplomacy between Russia and Ukraine, travelling to Moscow multiple times, and are expected to visit Kyiv this weekend. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Commentator Kethevane Gorjestani tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/eeb14596-a874-11f1-adb2-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260904-170306-170518-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/eeb14596-a874-11f1-adb2-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260904-170306-170518-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f3f23fb0-a874-11f1-88e3-79ef3788c04c</guid><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 15:29:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>On the ground: Russian drone strikes Ukraine security service headquarters in Kyiv</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-on-the-ground-russian-drone-strikes-ukraine-security-service-headquarters-in-kyiv</link><description>
A Russian drone struck the headquarters of Ukraine's SBU security services on Friday, Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky said, accusing Moscow of aiming directly at the SBU head's personal office. Zelensky said he had instructed the SBU to deliver an "appropriate, tangible response" to the strike, while Ukraine's Foreign Minister Andriy Sybiga described it as a "major escalation". FRANCE 24's Emmanuelle Chaze reports from Kyiv, Ukraine.
